Here is the SQL function to calculate the fan engagement score:

```sql
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION calculate_fan_engagement_score(
    statustag FanStatus_enum,
    tierstep SMALLINT,
    kindtag IdolType_enum,
    membkind MembershipType_enum,
    actfreq InteractionFrequency_enum,
    engrate DECIMAL(6,3),
    contqualrate DECIMAL(3,1),
    gifttot INT,
    giftvalusd DECIMAL(10,2),
    churnflag ChurnRisk_enum,
    loypts INT
) RETURNS DECIMAL(10,2) AS $
DECLARE
    engagement_score DECIMAL(10,2);
BEGIN
    -- Base engagement score calculation
    engagement_score := 0;

    -- Add points based on fan status
    CASE statustag
        WHEN 'VIP' THEN engagement_score := engagement_score + 100;
        WHEN 'Active' THEN engagement_score := engagement_score + 75;
        WHEN 'Inactive' THEN engagement_score := engagement_score + 25;
        WHEN 'Blocked' THEN engagement_score := engagement_score + 0;
    END CASE;

    -- Add points based on tier progression
    engagement_score := engagement_score + (tierstep * 10);

    -- Add points based on idol type
    CASE kindtag
        WHEN '2D' THEN engagement_score := engagement_score + 50;
        WHEN '3D' THEN engagement_score := engagement_score + 75;
        WHEN 'AI Generated' THEN engagement_score := engagement_score + 100;
        WHEN 'Mixed Reality' THEN engagement_score := engagement_score + 125;
    END CASE;

    -- Add points based on membership type
    CASE membkind
        WHEN 'Free' THEN engagement_score := engagement_score + 25;
        WHEN 'Basic' THEN engagement_score := engagement_score + 50;
        WHEN 'Premium' THEN engagement_score := engagement_score + 100;
        WHEN 'Diamond' THEN engagement_score := engagement_score + 150;
    END CASE;

    -- Add points based on interaction frequency
    CASE actfreq
        WHEN 'Daily' THEN engagement_score := engagement_score + 100;
        WHEN 'Weekly' THEN engagement_score := engagement_score + 75;
        WHEN 'Monthly' THEN engagement_score := engagement_score + 50;
        WHEN 'Occasional' THEN engagement_score := engagement_score + 25;
    END CASE;

    -- Add points based on engagement rate
    engagement_score := engagement_score + (engrate * 100);

    -- Add points based on content quality rate
    engagement_score := engagement_score + (contqualrate * 10);

    -- Add points based on gift total and value
    engagement_score := engagement_score + (gifttot * 5) + (giftvalusd * 0.1);

    -- Deduct points based on churn risk
    CASE churnflag
        WHEN 'High' THEN engagement_score := engagement_score - 100;
        WHEN 'Medium' THEN engagement_score := engagement_score - 50;
        WHEN 'Low' THEN engagement_score := engagement_score - 25;
        WHEN 'None' THEN engagement_score := engagement_score + 0;
    END CASE;

    -- Add points based on loyalty points
    engagement_score := engagement_score + (loypts * 0.01);

    -- Ensure the score is within a reasonable range (0-1000)
    engagement_score := GREATEST(0, LEAST(1000, engagement_score));

    RETURN engagement_score;
END;
$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;
```

This function takes various engagement metrics as inputs, including fan status, tier progression, idol type, membership type, interaction frequency, engagement rate, content quality rate, gift total and value, churn risk, and loyalty points. It calculates a weighted engagement score based on these metrics, ensuring the final score is within a reasonable range (0-1000).

**Note:** The weights and ranges used in this function are arbitrary and should be adjusted based on your specific requirements and data distribution. You may also want to consider adding more metrics or refining the existing ones to better capture fan engagement.

